WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.527
What's in an ACP deal report? Here's a real one, with the address and names grayed out.

2
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:09.857
First, the offer. One number to offer, and a walk-away ceiling.

3
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.976
The street view, with the after-repair value, repairs, price and as-is value.

4
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.373
The property record. Owner, liens to pay off, taxes, HOA, and flood zone.

5
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.995
Repairs, priced three ways. Minimum, realistic, and full scope.

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.327
After-repair value, from closed sales in the same subdivision.

7
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.337
Where it lists against the competition, and what it should sell for.

8
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.435
Financing. Your cash due at the offer, at the ceiling, and at the asking price.

9
00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.162
What to settle before you offer. Inspections, title, and insurance.

10
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.527
The as-is value, with the full county record.

11
00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.534
The flood zone, and a map of every comp.

12
00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:56.033
The comps. A hundred thirty-nine sales in the subdivision, sixty-eight matched on size and plan.

13
00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.098
And every repair line, priced three ways.

14
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:13.368
Financing and cash at closing. In Texas, at seventy percent of after-repair value, about twenty-eight thousand six hundred dollars is due. Outside Texas, at ninety-ten, about twenty-seven thousand six hundred.

15
00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:23.755
Estimated profit, based on the financing you qualify for. About twenty-one thousand dollars either way, roughly forty-one percent on your cash in six months.

16
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:30.156
Fix or rent? Fix it. As a rental, this house loses about seven hundred dollars a month.

17
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:40.801
Your own report is forty-nine ninety-nine, reimbursed in full if your deal closes with ACP. See the full sample at ACP lending dot com.
